{'symbol': 'ELV', 'date': '2023-03-03 11:22:00', 'title': "ELEVANCE HEALTH PUBLIC POLICY INSTITUTE'S STUDY ON LONG COVID PUBLISHED IN JAMA HEALTH FORUM STUDY", 'text': 'INDIANAPOLIS--(BUSINESS WIRE)--INDIVIDUALS WHO EXPERIENCE LONG COVID ARE AT INCREASED RISK FOR A WIDE RANGE OF ADVERSE CARDIOVASCULAR AND PULMONARY CONDITIONS AND MORTALITY, ACCORDING TO A NEW STUDY PUBLISHED IN JAMA HEALTH FORUM. THE STUDY, LED BY RESEARCHERS AT THE ELEVANCE HEALTH PUBLIC POLICY INSTITUTE, FOUND SUBSTANTIALLY HIGHER MORTALITY RATES FOR INDIVIDUALS WITH LONG COVID THAN WHAT HAD BEEN FOUND IN PREVIOUS STUDIES.'}